Sections "PROJECT" contain missmatched items: {'PROJECT_SUMMARY': ["Using samples from a randomized controlled trial conducted at Arkansas Children's Nutrition Center (NCT02125149), sedentary pregnant women with obesity were assigned to either a structured exercise intervention or standard prenatal care. Plasma collected immediately after submaximal treadmill exercise tests at 12 and 24 weeks of gestation was analyzed using untargeted LC-MS/MS metabolomics to characterize exercise-induced metabolic changes. A total of 401 annotated metabolites were detected across 119 participants. Longitudinal analysis identified significant pregnancy-related changes in 125 metabolites, including decreases in several acylcarnitines involved in energy metabolism and increases in metabolites associated with lipid absorption and metabolism. Two metabolites, nicotinamide and cis-13,14-methylene heptadecanoic acid, exhibited significant exercise-by-time interactions, with concentrations increasing during pregnancy only in the control group, while remaining stable in the exercise group. These findings suggest that regular prenatal exercise modifies metabolic adaptations to acute exercise and may prevent increases in metabolites associated with impaired metabolic health and insulin resistance.", "Using samples from a randomized controlled trial conducted at Arkansas Children''s Nutrition Center (NCT02125149), sedentary pregnant women with obesity were assigned to either a structured exercise intervention or standard prenatal care. Plasma collected immediately after submaximal treadmill exercise tests at 12 and 24 weeks of gestation was analyzed using untargeted LC-MS/MS metabolomics to characterize exercise-induced metabolic changes. A total of 401 annotated metabolites were detected across 119 participants. Longitudinal analysis identified significant pregnancy-related changes in 125 metabolites, including decreases in several acylcarnitines involved in energy metabolism and increases in